# Reopening a thread says what arrived while you were away.
#
# Without it a thread that gained twelve messages overnight looks exactly like
# one that gained none: you land at the bottom with no idea where to start.
#
# The divider sits before the first message newer than the stamp saved when the
# thread was last open. Marked read only once the newest message is actually on
# screen — marking on open would clear the very thing you opened it to see.
#
# NOTE: expect_no_text takes a BARE single word — see afterhours_gaps.md #47.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":[],"active_tab":"","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_BIG_TRANSCRIPT=1 HANABI_OPEN=rbig HANABI_UNREAD_DEMO=4

require_thread rbig

expect_text "4 new messages"

# Scrolling back through the thread does not un-read it or move the line.
key HOME
wait_frames 12
key END
wait_frames 12

# Still there after a round trip to the top and back: arriving at the end
# advances the stamp for NEXT time, it does not clear the line under you.
expect_text "4 new messages"
